WEBVTT

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:11.570
Too slow!

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.150
He cut down a demon in one blow...

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.460
Are we sure Matty-kun's human?

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.170
I'm so glad I'm not the enemy!

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.610
This is the same magic power reaction
as the spell from the palace,

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.130
and I can feel magic power...

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.090
...from two of them.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.690
One of them is probably Elhart.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.970
He shouldn't be a problem.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.060
The other one, however...

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.270
I'm sensing even more magic from him

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.560
than from the demons we fought before.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.530
However, things are different this time...

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.160
I've got all of my magic power now.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.280
Stop! You have to stop!

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.950
My apologies!

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.140
Are you okay?

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.290
Yeah, it's just been so long
since my last landing...

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.060
I'm not asking you, Iris.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.130
We're...

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.630
Fine.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:43.010
"Episode 4: The Strongest Sage Sneaks In"

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.340
They're probably inside.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:50.560
Can you hear me?

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:57.490
This is a telepathy spell that allows
conversation just by thinking, right?

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:57.990
Yup.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.000
I'll be using this to
communicate during the fight.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:02.200
Now then,

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:06.540
you two will be the main
attacking force in this fight.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:07.610
What?

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:09.110
There's no way! We can't!

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.030
That's what this magic seal is for.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:11.750
Besides,

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.460
you two will do just fine.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.090
Alright, let's go in.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:24.600
Huh?

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.700
There's no one here...

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:31.230
This is...

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:34.690
Okay you two, listen up.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:36.450
Yes!

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.110
The enemy is hiding.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.010
You can't see them because they're
using a concealment spell.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:41.820
Concealment?

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:46.830
The type they're using now can
completely conceal their magic power,

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:50.890
but now there are some suspicious
gaps in the magic, right?

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.250
Magic power...

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.930
Over there!

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.380
That's right.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.090
You're right, I can feel a
gap in the magic over there,

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:05.050
but I can't sense the other one.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.750
There are supposed to be two, right?

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.630
Yeah, but don't worry about that one

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.560
since we won't be able to find him for now.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.180
I'm going to throw a disruption
spell onto his concealment spell.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:16.020
Get ready.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.320
Okay, here we go.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:22.780
Now!

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:28.080
I've aimed an arrow at
him, but he's not moving?

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.540
Looks like he doesn't even know
he's not camouflaged anymore.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.540
Well, don't mind if I do then!

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.020
Impossible!

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.920
My disguise should have been impenetrable!

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.510
Clearly, it was not.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:48.820
Do you really think an arrow
would work on a demon?!

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.350
Just what are you trying to pull?!

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.260
Why won't you attack, you bastard?!

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:54.020
Aren't you the one they call Matthias?!

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:55.290
- Yeah, that would be me.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.230
- I see...
- Yeah, that would be me.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.680
It all makes sense!

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:01.230
If you were the real Matthias,
I'd already be dead!

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:04.070
That means you must be a fake!

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:04.700
Huh?

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.890
The real Matthias is in the Royal Capital.

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:08.690
There's no way he could be here!

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:09.860
- Now that I know you're not the
real thing, there's no need to hide!

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:12.260
- What the heck is he going on about?
- Now that I know you're not the
real thing, there's no need to hide!

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:12.870
- What the heck is he going on about?

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.330
I'll bury you here and now!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.040
I'll attack him head on.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.910
You two just hit him with
as many arrows as you can.

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:23.300
Y-You've got it!

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:23.800
Sure!

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.840
Do you really think you
can handle my attacks?

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:32.350
Phony or not, you're a decent
stand-in for the beast himself!

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.850
I told, I am the real thing!

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.020
Why you little...

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.570
Die, you phony!

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.240
Here's the next batch, Alma!

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.540
Such a pointless volley of attacks.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:55.000
You humans truly are weak creatures.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:58.330
Wha—

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.080
He's so fast!

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.010
No, that's not it.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.340
My body...

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.590
My movements are... slower...

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.430
I guess it finally kicked in.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:09.760
What?!

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.130
That magic seal was for Magitoxin.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:20.060
It interferes with a demon's magic,
and also inflicts rigidity.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:23.770
What's more, the poison accumulates,
and once it exceeds a certain amount,

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.030
the effects of the spell hit all at once.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:28.990
It... It can't be...

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:32.650
Me, lose to this fake?

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:34.600
Did you think...

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:37.910
...I'd allow... such a thing?!

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.250
What is that?

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.170
It's been a while since I've seen this.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.600
This is Atrocify, a spell demons
use when they're out of options.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:55.010
Once they've used all their magic
power, their life is forfeited...

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.280
They die?!

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:00.420
Damn you! Damn you, damn
you, damn you, damn you!

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:06.180
Yes, but in exchange, they get huge
boosts to magic power and strength.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.360
Kill...

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.360
This is bad.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:10.070
Run!

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:16.970
As if.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:20.330
That's how you use disguise magic.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.890
Damn it!

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.380
It wasn't just a simple illusion.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.760
They also delivered a
massive dose of Magitoxin.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:32.050
You're finished,

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.840
Elhart.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.660
We won?

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:47.280
I suppose that's one way to win a battle.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:49.020
You two did great.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.070
Excellent work.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:52.190
Yay!

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:53.210
Nice work.

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:54.670
You can leave the rest to me,

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:56.940
so go ahead and wait in the sky with Iris.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.830
What about you, Matty-kun?

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:00.710
The other demon...

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.920
...will be my opponent.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:07.250
I guess I should get started.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:10.460
First...

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:16.060
Crushing a Magistone releases
the magic power inside,

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:18.430
and causes a magic catastrophe.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:19.540
Second...

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:25.900
Under normal circumstances, that
would release a horde of monsters.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:27.650
Third.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:33.130
But if a mist demon happens to have
dispersed itself into the surrounding air,

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.910
this will force it to materialize.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:40.150
I certainly wasn't expecting you
to force me out of my mist form.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:42.830
Elhart called you a beast,

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.250
but even that doesn't seem
like a fitting nickname.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:48.260
That's not true.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:53.400
It wasn't my plan to bring you out by force,

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.010
but I didn't really have a choice.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:59.680
Well, if you went to the trouble of bringing
me here, you must be ready to die.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.860
I won't be as easy as Elhart.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.640
Oh, I know that,

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.130
but I don't plan on dying.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.820
Your plans won't matter once you're dead!

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:16.010
Well, he wasn't wrong.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.200
He's on a whole different level to Elhart.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.710
What happened to all that
boasting from earlier?

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.720
It's over now.

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:41.140
I suppose I can let you choose how you die.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:45.820
Sorry, but I don't plan on dying for
at least the next thousand years,

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:47.830
so I'll have to pass for now.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:48.980
What a brave face.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:50.730
Just a little more...

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.860
Let me put you out of your misery, then.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:55.610
Alright, analysis complete.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.700
Now, that's better.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.190
You... You really are a beast.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:05.450
How rude.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.580
I don't think he's noticed yet.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:11.810
I cast a restore spell on
my arm before he attacked.

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:14.420
That's not all.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.760
I cast an analysis spell on it too.

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:18.710
From the moment he cut it off,

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:21.470
I absorbed any and all
information about his powers.

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:23.180
Why can't I hit him?!

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:24.930
Don't you know?

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:28.020
I let you cut my arm off earlier.

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:36.070
This is...

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:38.780
...the poison that took Elhart out.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:41.240
Or so you think.

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:45.830
No matter, I'll end this quickly.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:48.850
Magic Power Channel Overclock!

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:53.630
It's similar to the spell Atrocify that
Elhart used, but even more powerful.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.670
What's more, it won't kill him afterwards.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:58.880
Now, this is where you die!

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:02.720
Come on, don't you want to spend
a little more time together?

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:06.470
Wh-What's going on?!

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:11.940
There shouldn't even be any spells
that can nullify that attack!

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:13.650
I wonder what happened.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:16.440
In that case...

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.010
It's over for you now!

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:30.410
Anyone who touches this mist will be
physically reduced to mist as well!

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:34.130
Certain death for those
without a counterspell.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:37.260
How did you nullify it?!

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.220
I'm the only one who can use this spell!

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.260
There's no way you could have a counterspell!

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:44.090
That's because I analyzed your magic.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:47.020
Once I figured out which
attack you would use,

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:49.060
I just had to plan my counterattack.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:50.380
Wha—

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:51.060
Oh dear.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:52.520
I guess it's time to wrap up.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:54.380
What is this?

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.980
That attack earlier wasn't poison.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.490
It was a spell to remove
your magic power control

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:02.990
so that you start collecting excess
magic from everything around you.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:06.700
Don't tell me, with no control
over my magic, I'll explode?

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:08.080
Correct.

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.870
I have a present for you.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:17.080
N-No, stop!

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:26.630
What?!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.560
Matty-kun...

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:40.320
As I suspected, this is what they were...

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.030
Matty-kun!

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:45.280
Lurie?!

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:50.580
I was so worried!

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.240
Are you okay?!

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:53.810
You're not hurt, are you?

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.750
No, I'm fine...

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.750
Thank goodness.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.260
Thanks for worrying about me.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.340
Are you two at it again?

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:08.930
Anyway, what's that?

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:12.380
Ah, that's a Dracopulse Pillar.

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:13.560
Dracopulse Pillar?

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:17.750
Dracopulses are streams of magic
that flow throughout the land.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:22.060
Dracopulse Pillars are used to
control the flow of that energy.

00:13:22.060 --> 00:13:24.050
Based on these seals on this one,

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:27.570
it seems they were planning to
call a large horde of monsters.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:28.680
What?!

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:33.060
I say horde, but it's only about 5,000 of those
level 10 monsters from the Royal Capital's dungeon.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.210
Oh, and some bosses.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:35.540
F-Five thousand?!

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:39.350
Yeah, and the demons were likely hiding here

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:43.550
to control the Dracopulse until they were
ready to unleash the horde somewhere.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:46.010
When you say somewhere, you mean...

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.510
I've got a bad feeling about his answer.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:49.890
Yup,

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:51.600
the Royal Capital.

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:54.760
A horde of monsters in the capital?!

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:55.980
It would be a massacre!

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:59.570
We've got to hurry back to evacuate the city!

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:01.190
There's no need to panic just yet.

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:04.170
Thanks to that explosion, a
lot of magic's been dispersed,

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:07.650
so the current site has probably moved 10
or so kilometers away from the capital.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.680
Is that what that big explosion
was all about before?

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.260
Did you predict this happening too?

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.500
It's only 10 kilometers, though.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.710
I've already got a plan.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:17.440
What?

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:20.190
I'll need some help from the academy,

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:22.170
but we should be able
to make a counterattack.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.170
I'll share the details later on.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.630
Let's head back for now.

00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:30.340
We should make it back before sunset.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:32.550
Umm...

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:36.790
Any idea what I should
be doing in the meantime?

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:39.510
Now that you mention it,
I hadn't really thought about it.

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:43.460
Isn't there a spell that
gives dragons human form?

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:45.190
Can you use it now?

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:49.740
Yes, casting such a spell would use
very little magic power at all.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.280
I've never really used it before, though.

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:55.150
In that case, would you like
to join us at the academy?

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:55.790
Huh?

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:59.770
There probably isn't much for you to learn,

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:03.440
but if you enter the academy,
you'll be able to stick with us.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:05.500
It'll be easier to heal you as well.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:09.770
Plus, I'll have a convenient
means of transport.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:13.550
I know absolutely nothing
about human academies...

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:17.780
We already have a socially awkward
eccentric at the school, so it's fine.

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:22.490
Though we've probably been hanging
out with him a lot lately.

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:26.130
See? There are already some weirdos around.

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:28.020
Not that I know any of them.

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:31.360
In that case, I'll get started.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:38.080
Good,

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.580
looks like we don't need to
make any adjustments for age.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.940
Hold on, that's a girl!

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:44.270
Matty-kun, don't stare at her!

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:45.540
- What's going on?
- Just what do you think you're doing, Matty-kun?!

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:46.850
- H-Hey!
- Just what do you think you're doing, Matty-kun?!

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:48.110
Quit it! Iris is just a dragon!

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:50.010
Even so!

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:55.720
These are horns taken from Elhart's body.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:16:00.660
You defeated demons several thousands
of kilometers away in mere days.

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:02.630
It won't be long before you take every item

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:05.360
in the treasure house as a reward.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.820
We can worry about the demons later.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:10.360
For now, I have a favor to ask.

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:13.230
That would be something only
you could worry about later.

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:14.400
What is it?

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:17.360
I'd like you to grant her
admission to the academy.

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:19.080
I'm Iris.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.840
A new admission?

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:24.130
She can certainly apply, but she
won't get any special treatment.

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:26.590
She still has to take the admission exam.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:27.930
Of course.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.840
Also, our standards are pretty high.

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.710
The exam is the same as the entrance exam,

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:36.290
but you need 47 points out of 50 to pass.

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:38.350
That's almost a perfect score!

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:40.060
Not a problem.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.390
Though I have a request...

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.650
Would I be able to observe the exams?

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:47.570
It's just as a precaution.

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:49.110
I won't interfere with the exam.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:51.430
I don't have a problem with that, although...

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:53.320
...what precautions?

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:56.180
Iris has only recently taken human form,

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:58.780
so she probably can't
control her magic just yet.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:02.630
I'd better take precautions in case
her dragon powers go a little crazy...

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:07.380
She could destroy the entire campus
before she makes it to her first class.

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:10.880
It's up to you now, Iris.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:16.800
When will you tell him about the Dracopulse
Pillar and the horde of monsters?

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:19.310
Well, we wouldn't want everyone to panic,

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:22.430
so I'll probably wait until
Iris finishes her exam.

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.440
We still have plenty of time.

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:26.400
A very Matty-kun-style priority list!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:28.770
This could get pretty annoying.

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:30.510
You'll have to live with it.

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:32.480
Humans have to wear clothes, after all.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:36.320
Speaking of which, give
me your left hand, Iris.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:43.330
You know how to make crests too, Matty-kun?

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.970
It's just a simple decoration,

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:48.290
similar to the ones used
by the demons we defeated.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:49.600
Ohh...

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.290
Good luck with your exam tomorrow!

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:52.750
Oh, sure.

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:57.760
You may begin the written exam.

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:08.590
Oh no...

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:10.040
Iris-san...

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:12.940
I think I underestimated dragon eccentricity.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:15.170
Hey, Matthias...

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:16.470
Don't worry.

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:18.530
She's got real talent.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.620
Next, we'll move on to the practical exam.

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:24.010
Matthias Hildesheimer,

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:27.910
I can't wait to see how strong
this friend you've recommended is!

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.890
Who is that again?

00:18:30.890 --> 00:18:33.380
He was your opponent during
your entrance exam,

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:35.410
Guile-san, the knight captain.

00:18:35.410 --> 00:18:36.880
Now that you mention it,

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.720
he does seem rather knightly.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:40.760
You have no idea who he is, do you?!

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.720
This could be dangerous...

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:46.180
...for her opponent.

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:48.440
Begin the swordsmanship exam!

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:53.850
Huh?

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.990
Oh, could you wait just a moment?

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:59.490
Don't you turn your back on the battlefield!

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:04.080
I asked you to wait a moment.

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:06.660
She stopped it... bare-handed?

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.350
She didn't even budge an inch!

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:10.880
How strong is that tiny little girl?!

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:13.780
In a swordsmanship exam,

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:15.920
I have to beat you with a sword, right?

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:16.920
What?!

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:19.930
This is bad!

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:22.970
Here we... go!

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.020
Oh dear, I broke it.

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:32.170
What happens now?

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:33.900
She can't be serious...

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:38.080
Hey, are you sure this is just a young girl?

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:39.990
Yes, it's just a young girl.

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:42.800
Who happens to be a dragon.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.200
Next is the magic exam.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:53.260
The targets are so small.

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:00.050
Here goes nothing.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:08.810
And there she goes!

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:20.470
It was... deflected?

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.590
Come on, Iris.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:24.450
S-Sorry!

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:26.700
I've got it this time!

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:40.850
Now that's odd...

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:43.300
The only odd thing is the
power behind those spells!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:43.730
"Calamity"

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:44.680
Is she some sort of calamity-class monster?!
"Calamity"

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.270
Is she some sort of calamity-class monster?!

00:20:46.270 --> 00:20:48.310
Oh well,

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.890
I guess I'll have to do it the
way Matthias-san told me to.

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:53.700
Here we go.

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:57.360
Just as I thought...

00:20:57.360 --> 00:21:00.160
What is she trying to do now?

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:01.820
You'll see.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.210
I'll hit them this time.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:15.670
Iris-san...

00:21:18.930 --> 00:21:21.470
I've destroyed all the targets!

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:23.340
What do you think?

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:25.540
She sure is...

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:27.050
A Dark Dragon!

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:28.960
What do you think?

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:31.930
I think this whole thing
is... completely absurd.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:36.720
I can't very well fail
her, but also... Well...

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:39.070
I suppose...

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:41.980
You pass!

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:43.410
Yay!

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:45.800
You did it, Iris-san!

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:49.870
Our poor courtyard...

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.940
I'll fix it.

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:30.340
Today, I'll be interviewing Iris, who made
the giant crater in the school courtyard!

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:32.900
How in the world did it end up like this?

00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:36.430
Well, I just gathered up
all my power and BOOM.

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:37.020
It just happened.

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:38.030
"Episode 5: The Strongest Sage Gains a Friend"
It just happened.

00:23:38.030 --> 00:23:38.610
"Episode 5: The Strongest Sage Gains a Friend"
Teehee!

00:23:38.610 --> 00:23:40.020
"Episode 5: The Strongest Sage Gains a Friend"
Don't give me "teehee"!
